WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.136 --> 00:00:08.179
WearAgain: your wardrobe, your stylist, a reason to buy less. This walkthrough uses saved examples, not fresh API calls.

2
00:00:08.179 --> 00:00:15.190
Start with what you own. See your pieces and whether they are ready, in the wash or awaiting repair.

3
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:20.248
Describe an occasion in your own words. This demo prepares verified wardrobe recipes; live AI interpretation is a future integration.

4
00:00:20.248 --> 00:00:26.306
An illustrative full look sits beside the actual wardrobe pieces. Genuine single-garment recordings remain separately inspectable.

5
00:00:26.306 --> 00:00:32.408
Save an outfit, open it again and record it as worn. Availability is checked before reuse.

6
00:00:32.408 --> 00:00:39.420
Assign a saved look to a trip occasion. The packing list contains the pieces you selected, without duplicates.

7
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:46.440
Before buying, compare two genuine saved YouCam previews: one shop garment and one owned top. They are separate renders.

8
00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:52.484
Your wear / do-not-wear ratings feed the minimum-basket solver. The recommended basket uses the sample prices and stated needs.

9
00:00:52.484 --> 00:00:58.609
Sometimes the best basket is empty. This separate example proves that existing pieces can cover all stated needs.

10
00:00:58.609 --> 00:01:04.672
Shopping without waiting: collect photos, review over coffee and keep a return list by shop and floor. Here the previews are saved examples.

11
00:01:04.672 --> 00:01:09.688
Return only for the pieces you shortlisted. Live previews require explicit opt-in; this recording makes no provider requests.

12
00:01:09.688 --> 00:01:15.724
Your wardrobe dashboard: recorded wear history, readiness and decisions to keep, repair, sell or pass on.

13
00:01:15.724 --> 00:01:21.760
For retailers: an illustrative product page with wardrobe context. This is a demonstration, not a merchant checkout.

14
00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:27.768
For judges: a three-step guided demo with genuine API provenance and a reproducible decision certificate. Style preview, not size fit.
